                <pb facs="0535" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg455"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jackson to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-07-05"><hi rendition="#italic">July 5,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1998.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence, I
                    have the honor to inform you that a note has just been received from the German
                    foreign office in which it is stated that permission is granted the Eisemann
                    brothers to remain in Frankfort-on-the-Main until the 1st of next April.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
